Twinkle Star — credits for third-party material

Text
- "The Star" ("Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star"), first verse, by Jane Taylor (1806). Public domain.

Music
- Original score written for this film. The closing music-box tune is the traditional melody
  "Ah! vous dirai-je, maman" (18th-century French folk tune). Public domain.
- All instruments are synthesized in code (Karplus–Strong nylon guitar and modal music box from
  core/audio/pluck.py; bells, foley and ambience from numpy / core/audio/sfx.py). No samples used.

Voice
- Kokoro TTS (kokoro-onnx, model kokoro-v1.0), voice "af_heart". Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx · https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/)
- Patrick Hand by Patrick Wagesreiter. https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/patrickhand
- Gaegu by JIKJI SOFT. https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/gaegu

Picture
- Drawn entirely in code with the Crayon Picture Book engine (gl.js, crayon.js, rig.js) from the
  Lemo-Opuscar style library (see the library's LICENSE).
